# Artifact style profile — {{PROJECT_NAME}}

Consumed by the local-first artifact flow (`rules/artifacts-local-first.md`,
step B.2) for every HTML artifact/report generated in this project.

**This file is a DELTA, not a design system.** The design system is the kit —
`~/.claude/skills/aidex-dash/assets/artifact-kit/` — which `wrap-report.sh`
injects into every artifact. Of everything below, the wrapper reads exactly
three things: the `css` fence in `## Delta`, `Favicon emoji:`, and `language:`.
The rest is prose for whoever writes the page; filling in the palette table
below changes nothing on its own. Delete any section you don't want to
constrain.

## Palette

| Token | Light | Dark | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| ground | #FFFFFF | #14181C | page background |
| ink | #1F2A31 | #DAE2E4 | body text |
| accent | #116B5F | #52B0A0 | one accent, used sparingly |
| good / warn / critical | — | — | semantic states, distinct from accent |

The table is documentation. To actually restyle the pages, put the same values
in `## Delta` below as CSS, in BOTH blocks — the kit ships a dark palette of its
own, and a delta that only redefines the light one leaves the page half-restyled:

```css
:root { --accent: #116B5F; }
:root[data-theme="dark"] { --accent: #52B0A0; }
```

That fence is an EXAMPLE and is not injected, because it sits here rather than
under `## Delta`. That is the whole reason the rule is scoped to a section.

