## Delta

The one section `wrap-report.sh` reads as CSS. It injects the FIRST `css` fence
inside this section, after the kit and before the page's own styles, so anything
here overrides the kit and nothing here has to restate it. A project whose
identity IS the kit's leaves the fence as it stands.

```css
/* No delta yet: this project uses the kit's own identity. */
```

Only override tokens here — the kit's components read every colour and font
stack from them, so changing values restyles the whole system without touching
a single rule. And keep worked examples OUT of this section: whatever sits in
the first fence here becomes the project's real palette.

## Language

- language: en

Read as a field, not as prose: `wrap-report.sh` parses the first `language:`
line in this file and uses it as the document's `<html lang>` when no explicit
`--lang` is passed. Precedence is `--lang` > this field > `en`.

Scope is ARTIFACTS only. `.context/` stays English (D-04) whatever this says —
it is a historical record and is cheaper to search in one language — and
`communications/` bodies stay in the language they arrived in. This field
exists so a project whose reader wants Spanish reports configures it once here
instead of restating it per request.
